  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Calabresella. Logic: See rules.objective and rules.gameplay.',
    Player: 'Calabresella (also known as Terziglio) is an Italian three-player point-trick game with bidding. It is closely related to Tressette. The main aim is to capture aces and take the last trick, which is difficult because there are no trumps. The game features an unusual card order with threes as the highest cards.',
    objective: 'Capture aces (worth 1 point each) and win the last trick (worth 1 point). Total 5 points per hand. First to 11 or 21 points wins the game.',
    gameplay: 'The game is a point-trick game with bidding. Players bid to determine who plays alone against the other two. The bidder must capture at least 3 of the 5 available points (the four aces and the last trick). Cards are played in tricks with no trumps. Players must follow suit if possible. Highest card of led suit wins the trick. Winner leads to next trick.',
